WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.549
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:11.070
I was in the seventh grade, and it was
the day before the animal science fair.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.629
Now, I was the undisputed
Queen of the science field.

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:20.190
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Not because I was a science nerd, but

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.880
because I had a very innovative model.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.740
And this time, we have made
a beautiful model of the solar system.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.310
Not only were the planets
scaled to perfection, but

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.100
they also rotated around the sun as
we had a small motor in the center.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.430
That motor had cost me
all my pocket money.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.560
Now midnight before the big day,
I thought I just tried one last time.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.920
I flip the on switch and it didn't work.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:54.090
My heart beating faster I tried
it again and again, but nothing.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.310
I shouted for my mum and
she came running inside the room.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:00.130
She took one look at the model and
understood the problem.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:06.090
Looking around the room she thought for a
minute, she then smiled, turned around and

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.650
remove the clock from the ward.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.760
She unscrewed the hands carefully and
pasted the sun in the center.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.840
She flicked the on switch.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.760
It was magic.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.606
It was incredibly.

00:01:19.606 --> 00:01:23.900
Now this moment of
ingenuity fascinated me.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.830
Why hadn't I thought of
the clock instead of that

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.430
bulky noisy motor in the first place?

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:35.150
I realized that this creativity had only
been possible due to the force time and

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.270
resource constraints.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:42.729
Over the years, I observed this process
several times across many incidents and

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:44.904
identified a very strange theme.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:49.460
Creativity loves constraints.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.230
And why is that?

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:54.220
Fewer constraints means more choice.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.250
And choice is paralyzing.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.460
We humans are terrible at decision making.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.520
How many of you have given
up on watching the movie

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.275
after spending hours
flicking through Netflix?

00:02:06.275 --> 00:02:09.527
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Constraints actually give

00:02:09.527 --> 00:02:11.970
us the building blocks to
start experimenting with.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.070
In a recent experiment participants
were divided into two groups and

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.120
asked to compose rhymes.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.730
One group was given a set of eight
randomly generated nouns and

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.140
the other group was free to use
whichever words they wanted.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:31.210
&gt;&gt; Judges evaluated their rhymes and
was surprised to find that the group

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.950
that was working under constraints
had more creative, more novel times.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.970
Yes, creativity loves constraints.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:44.350
In India, often capital and regulatory
constraints are a way of life for

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.830
entrepreneurs and creativity thrives.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.040
We even have a Hindi word for that.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.300
It's called Jugaad.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:57.910
Jugaad is a flexible approach to problem
solving that stems from a can do attitude.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:02.655
It is a mental leap that permits one to
accept that challenge of constraint and

00:03:02.655 --> 00:03:05.363
leads to destructive designs in products.

00:03:05.363 --> 00:03:08.010
And this concept is not just Indian.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.570
Take the example of Israel,
a nation that has combated war and

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:16.630
intelligence with unparalleled innovation,
earning it the name startup nation.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:21.009
During a study trip I interacted with
local entrepreneurs and I was surprised

00:03:21.009 --> 00:03:25.402
to find that they actually attributed
Israel successes to its constraints.

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:31.900
But I also heard stories, where the
concept of Jugaag was met with disdain and

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:32.640
rejection.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.500
While working in Mumbai,

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.840
my favorite hangout place was this rooftop
restaurant opposite my office building.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.720
One night, there was a massive
fire that destroyed the place.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:50.353
It was a horrific incident 14 people died.

00:03:50.353 --> 00:03:55.784
The reason had been an illegal bamboo
roof structure that caught fire easily.

00:03:55.784 --> 00:03:58.833
The owners were not able to
get the approvals on time and

00:03:58.833 --> 00:04:02.220
had resorted to this quick fix
to deal with that constraint.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.500
Four weeks after that,
I could see the side ashes and

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.610
the wood remains of the rooftop
front of window near my work desk.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.080
It was a painful bench that
served as a constant reminder

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.290
that working around constraints could
lead to disastrous consequences.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:25.360
I lost strong hope Jugaad was going
to be overtaken, watered down and

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.510
used as an excuse for sloppy thinking.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:33.290
And this grace Smith's application
of creativity makes me angry.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.920
If you can make a low quality,
dangerous product at a low budget,

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.680
how is that creativity?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.120
If you can break the law to deal with
that constraint, how is that creativity.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.940
Creativity is that handheld ECG
monitor made by GE scientists at

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.960
a fraction of the original cost, but has
saved millions of lives in rural India.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.730
Creativity is a beautiful baby
incubator made by GSB alumni,

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:03.150
which had to be made
at a fraction of cost.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.130
It was even better than the original
concept because it allowed the mother to

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.444
hold the baby while it
was being incubated.

00:05:11.819 --> 00:05:13.586
While working in Mumbai,

00:05:13.586 --> 00:05:19.830
I was working on a development project
to increase literacy in rural Rajasthan.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.090
And I came across a tricky problem.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.300
I noticed that students were
unable to go to school and

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:30.350
have continued education because they
were traveling for several months.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.860
They traveled on camel back for several
days at a stretch with their tribes and

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.620
communities.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.800
Now given the limited
funds at my disposal,

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:42.220
I could not solve this problem by going
about building schools in the desert.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.640
I considered using technology and
maybe providing tablets to the tribes.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.010
But the because of the limited
access to electricity and

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.740
internet, this would have never worked.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.715
Given the cost, and technology, and
location constraints, I needed a Jugaad.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.270
But dashes was still fresh in my memory.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.933
I needed a solution that could
speak to my concept of Jugaad.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:10.017
I needed a solution that could work
within the constraints and yet

00:06:10.017 --> 00:06:13.000
trumped the traditional solution
in its quality and utility.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.510
Identifying the problem I thought
that if the kids could not

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:22.880
go to school because they were traveling
what if the school went with them.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.590
We designed the idea of a mobile school,

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.210
which was a simple cart on
wheels furnished with books,

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:34.250
chart paper or Blackboard, and then we
trained a few teachers in every community.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.220
Things fell into place.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:44.220
This initiative transformed
the lives of nomadic communities.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.360
We realized that not just kids
even the adults had a lot of

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.250
idle time while travelling for
days at a stretch.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.830
This easy access to books and
teachers stole their curiosity and

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.520
they started attending
the modern school as well.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:00.020
With the cascading effect the entire
community started becoming literate.

00:07:02.397 --> 00:07:06.136
Next time when you are faced
with an innovation challenge,

00:07:06.136 --> 00:07:10.918
be it to design a new product, launch
a new strategy, or even to prepare your

00:07:10.918 --> 00:07:16.660
evening meal, I invite you to think about
my story and try these three steps.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.370
One, identify the underlying need.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:22.340
For us, the need was not building schools.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:23.710
It was educating the children.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.220
Two recognize your constraints.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:30.030
We needed a solution that would
work within our location,

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.210
time capital constraints.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:36.170
And if there aren't any constraints
fit yourself with seemingly

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:40.714
unattainable goals in terms of delivery
time, functionality or inputs.

00:07:40.714 --> 00:07:44.530
Challenge yourself to prepare that
meal with just four ingredients.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:48.165
Challenge yourself to sketch that
first prototype in one hour and

00:07:48.165 --> 00:07:49.496
experiment with that.

00:07:49.496 --> 00:07:52.320
Remember, creativity loves constraints.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.705
Three and the most important believe
that you can solve the problem.

00:07:57.705 --> 00:08:02.220
Jugaad thinking is a leap of faith that
needs a lot of experimentation and

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.600
may result in failure.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.330
So brace yourself.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.210
We did not know if the community
would even accept the solution

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:11.180
of a school traveling with them,
but they welcomed it.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.665
An year after the launch, an 85 year old
man from the community wrote me a letter.

00:08:17.665 --> 00:08:20.715
It said, because of you,

00:08:20.715 --> 00:08:25.297
no one will say that I died illiterate.

00:08:25.297 --> 00:08:28.450
Feeling that letter my faith
in Jugaad thinking was reborn.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:33.340
A Jugaad is what allowed me to
impact him and thousands of others.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.750
Jugaad was that aha moment when I
solved the puzzle of constraints.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:43.070
A Jugaad is that gift my mom gave me when
she solved my model years and years ago.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.760
A Jugaad is my offering to you.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.486
And next time when you are faced
with an innovation challenge,

00:08:49.486 --> 00:08:54.000
shackle yourself with constraints and
unleash the freedom of creativity.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:54.711
Thank you.

00:08:54.711 --> 00:08:56.463
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:08:56.463 --> 00:09:01.094
[MUSIC]

